#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkBatchedLabeledDataMapper-implementation.md:1
msgid "vtkBatchedLabeledDataMapper: Implementation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkBatchedLabeledDataMapper-implementation.md:3
msgid "Background"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkBatchedLabeledDataMapper-implementation.md:5
msgid ""
"`vtkFastLabeledDataMapper` was introduced in VTK 9.5 as a faster replacement "
"for `vtkLabeledDataMapper`. Instead of issuing one draw call per label, it "
"packs all glyphs into a single texture atlas and emits them in one geometry-"
"shader pass, making label-heavy scenes significantly cheaper to render. Its "
"initial implementation lived entirely in `Rendering/OpenGL2`, which tied the "
"atlas-building logic to the OpenGL backend and made it impossible to reuse "
"the same approach on other backends or in non-3D contexts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkBatchedLabeledDataMapper-implementation.md:13
msgid "New class: vtkBatchedLabeledDataMapper"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkBatchedLabeledDataMapper-implementation.md:15
msgid ""
"`vtkBatchedLabeledDataMapper` is a `vtkLabeledDataMapper` subclass that "
"brings the same glyph-atlas batch rendering to both world-space and display-"
"space label overlays. It inherits the full API of `vtkLabeledDataMapper` "
"(coordinate systems, transform, label mode, text properties) but replaces "
"the one-draw-call-per-label rendering with a glyph atlas batch approach so "
"that all labels are drawn in a single pass."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkBatchedLabeledDataMapper-implementation.md:22
msgid "It follows a backend-split architecture:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkBatchedLabeledDataMapper-implementation.md:24
msgid ""
"**`vtkBatchedLabeledDataMapper`** (`Rendering/Label`) — backend-agnostic "
"base class that accepts any `vtkDataSet`, builds the glyph atlas, and "
"prepares the per-label geometry arrays."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkBatchedLabeledDataMapper-implementation.md:27
msgid ""
"**`vtkOpenGLBatchedLabeledDataMapper`** (`Rendering/OpenGL2`) — OpenGL "
"backend that uploads the atlas to a `vtkTextureObject` and renders all "
"labels in one geometry-shader pass using a `vtkOpenGLPolyDataMapper` helper."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkBatchedLabeledDataMapper-implementation.md:30
msgid ""
"**`vtkWebGPUBatchedLabeledDataMapper`** (`Rendering/WebGPU`) — WebGPU "
"backend using instanced rendering: 18 vertices per label instance (3 layers "
"× 6 vertices) with WGSL shader replacements for atlas sampling, background, "
"and frame rendering."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkBatchedLabeledDataMapper-implementation.md:35
msgid "The API extends `vtkLabeledDataMapper` with two additions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkBatchedLabeledDataMapper-implementation.md:37
msgid ""
"**`TextAnchor`** — positions the label bounding box relative to its screen "
"point (`LowerLeft`, `UpperRight`, `Center`, etc.)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkBatchedLabeledDataMapper-implementation.md:39
msgid ""
"**`DisplayOffset`** — applies a fixed pixel nudge `(dx, dy)` to every label "
"in display space, useful for pushing labels away from their anchor point."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkBatchedLabeledDataMapper-implementation.md:42
msgid ""
"vtkNew<vtkBatchedLabeledDataMapper> mapper;\n"
"mapper->SetLabelModeToLabelFieldData();\n"
"mapper->SetFieldDataName(\"names\");\n"
"// drive per-label text property selection from the \"types\" array\n"
"mapper->SetInputArrayToProcess(\n"
"  0, 0, 0, vtkDataObject::FIELD_ASSOCIATION_POINTS, \"types\");\n"
"mapper->SetLabelTextProperty(prop0, 0);\n"
"mapper->SetLabelTextProperty(prop1, 1);\n"
"mapper->SetTextAnchor(vtkBatchedLabeledDataMapper::LowerLeft);\n"
"int offset[2] = { 4, 4 };\n"
"mapper->SetDisplayOffset(offset);\n"
"mapper->SetInputData(dataset);\n"
"\n"
"vtkNew<vtkActor2D> actor;\n"
"actor->SetMapper(mapper);\n"
"renderer->AddViewProp(actor);\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkBatchedLabeledDataMapper-implementation.md:61
msgid "Breaking change: vtkLabeledDataMapper::Implementation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkBatchedLabeledDataMapper-implementation.md:63
msgid ""
"The protected data member `Implementation` in `vtkLabeledDataMapper` has "
"been changed from a raw pointer (`Internals* Implementation`) to a `std::"
"unique_ptr<Internals>`. Subclasses that stored or transferred ownership of "
"this pointer must be updated accordingly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkBatchedLabeledDataMapper-implementation.md:68
msgid "Deprecation of vtkFastLabeledDataMapper"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkBatchedLabeledDataMapper-implementation.md:70
msgid ""
"`vtkFastLabeledDataMapper` (the original `vtkOpenGLPolyDataMapper`-based 3D "
"label mapper in `Rendering/OpenGL2`) is deprecated as of VTK 9.7. Use "
"`vtkBatchedLabeledDataMapper` instead, which supports both world-space and "
"display-space rendering and works across all backends via the object factory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkBatchedLabeledDataMapper-implementation.md:75
msgid "vtkGridAxesActor2D: batch tick label rendering"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkBatchedLabeledDataMapper-implementation.md:77
msgid ""
"`vtkGridAxesActor2D` now uses `vtkBatchedLabeledDataMapper` for tick labels. "
"Previously, each tick mark on each axis edge was backed by an individual "
"`vtkBillboardTextActor3D`, meaning the renderer issued one draw call per "
"visible tick on every frame. Each of the four axis edges now owns a single "
"`vtkBatchedLabeledDataMapper` fed by a per-edge `vtkPolyData`, so the entire "
"set of tick labels for an edge is rendered in one batched pass. Title labels "
"remain as `vtkBillboardTextActor3D` actors since there is at most one per "
"edge."
msgstr ""
